==========================================
DAY 05 NOTES — Networking Basics
Date: 01-09-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- Private IPs (192.168.x.x, 10.x.x.x) stay inside a local network; public IPs are internet-visible
- Ports are numbered "doors" — 22=SSH, 80=HTTP, 443=HTTPS, 21=FTP
- ping checks "is it alive", ss/netstat checks "what's open on THIS machine", curl checks "what does it say back"
- ss -tuln shows listening ports; add -p (needs sudo) to see which process owns each port
- Ping getting blocked (no response) doesn't always mean a server is actually down
- curl -I gets headers/status code only, without downloading the full page

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] ip addr show / hostname -I
[ ] ping -c 4
[ ] ss -tuln / ss -tulnp
[ ] curl -I / curl api.ipify.org
[ ] dig +short

Fill this in after running commands yourself :
$ ip addr show
> 

$ ping -c 4 google.com
> 

$ ss -tuln
> 


